{
  "_": "The JSON K2 reads from tauri-plugin-sew-voice's video commands and events (prd-sew-62 §B7). src-tauri's native_voice::tests holds this file to the plugin's real types at the pinned commit (Sew 0.8.2: commands, events, every payload, the refusal codes and the stop reasons; no_frames is Sew 0.8.3's, listed ahead); native-video-engine.test.ts holds the TS adapter to this file.",
  "decisions": [
    "command arguments are snake_case (sink_id)",
    "video_sink's sink_id is a u32 number (the frame header's); codec is null in decoded mode, and also in encoded mode for a self-view sink opened before the camera or preview runs",
    "permission is 'granted' | 'denied' (covers the OS's restricted case) | 'prompt' | 'unsupported' (no such capture on this OS or build)",
    "the plugin never asks for the camera itself: camera_permission reads it, request_camera_permission (only on the person's button press) asks; camera {on} without it rejects camera_permission_not_determined or camera_permission_denied",
    "screen_sources[].thumbnail_png is standard base64 with no data: prefix, at most 320 px wide; kind is 'display' | 'window'",
    "policy is sew-proto's MediaPolicy JSON; the UI reads video_enabled, camera_allowed and screen_allowed (absent reads as true)",
    "there is no pick_screen: screen {on: true} with no source opens the OS picker; with a source it shares that id; the plugin passes the Windows window handle itself",
    "video_caps always exists; a build without video answers with everything off and backend 'null' (older plugins reject it); receive, self_view and live_switch are missing in an older payload and read as false",
    "every start of frames (open, visible false to true, unmute, layer change, request_keyframe, loss recovery) begins at a keyframe with the discontinuity flag",
    "stats are cumulative; every 10 s is fine",
    "the renderer draws straight to a canvas; there is no MediaStream, so no picture-in-picture from it (native sinks and PiP are phone-only)",
    "a hidden or minimised window pauses a screen share: local_video {screen: 'paused', reason: 'hidden'}"
  ],
